   "eligible": true,
   "waitYears": 2,
   "waitFrom": "discharge of the sentence",
   "automatic": true,
   "note": "A misdemeanor can be expunged by petition after 2 years without a new conviction; since January 1, 2025, most misdemeanors are expunged automatically after the same period. Gross misdemeanors wait 3 years.",
   "citation": "Minn. Stat. §§ 609A.02, subd. 3; 609A.015",
   "source_url": "https://ccresourcecenter.org/state-restoration-profiles/minnesota-restoration-of-rights-pardon-expungement-sealing/",
