   "waitYears": 4,
   "waitFrom": "discharge of the sentence",
   "automatic": true,
   "note": "About 50 listed lower-level felonies (mostly theft, fraud and drug offenses) can be expunged after 4 years without a new conviction, by petition or automatically since 2025. Felonies not on the list cannot be expunged except by pardon.",
   "citation": "Minn. Stat. §§ 609A.02, subd. 3(b); 609A.015",
   "source_url": "https://ccresourcecenter.org/state-restoration-profiles/minnesota-restoration-of-rights-pardon-expungement-sealing/",
