   "automatic": false,
   "note": "You can ask the court to set aside a conviction once you finish a sentence of probation, a fine, community service, or jail of 1 year or less. There is no waiting period. Set-aside 'nullifies' the conviction but does not seal or erase the record, which can still be used for sentence enhancement.",
   "citation": "Neb. Rev. Stat. § 29-2264(2)-(5)",
   "source_url": "https://ccresourcecenter.org/state-restoration-profiles/nebraska-restoration-of-rights-pardon-expungement-sealing/",
